.TH SERIAL 3 "2026" "y-- standard library" "y-- Library Reference"
.SH NAME
Serial \- serial port (UART) communication
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B Serial
module opens serial ports (UART) for reading and writing.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.SS open
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
SerialObj() open(port: string(), baud: int())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Opens the serial port at
.I port
with baud rate
.IR baud .
On POSIX configures 8N1 via tcsetattr with 0.5s read timeout.
On Windows configures via DCB with 50ms timeouts.
Returns a SerialObj handle with methods:
.RS
.TP
read(n: int()) -> string()
Reads up to n bytes.
.TP
write(data: string()) -> int()
Writes data, returns bytes written.
.TP
close() -> none()
Closes the port.
.RE
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
\fBRuntimeError\fR \- port cannot be opened.
.TP
\fBEXAMPLES\fR
.EX
s = Serial.open("/dev/ttyUSB0", 9600)
s.write("hello")
data = s.read(64)
s.close()
.EE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
Socket(3)
